# area: Agent safety
mission AgentToolAuthorization

goal
  Decide whether an agent may call a tool within an approved permission scope.

why
  A model proposal must pass the same permission check as a human action.

guarantee tool access requires a valid permission scope
  verify test ToolAccess

never allow a write without explicit approval
  verify test ToolAccess

decision ToolAccess
  inputs
    scopeAllowed
    isWrite
    approved
  rule read within scope
    when scopeAllowed == true and isWrite == false
    return Allow
  rule approved write within scope
    when scopeAllowed == true and isWrite == true and approved == true
    return Allow
  default
    return Deny

test ToolAccess
  case scoped read
    given scopeAllowed true, isWrite false, approved false
    expect Allow
  case unapproved write
    given scopeAllowed true, isWrite true, approved false
    expect Deny
  case approved write
    given scopeAllowed true, isWrite true, approved true
    expect Allow
  case out of scope read
    given scopeAllowed false, isWrite false, approved false
    expect Deny
  case approval cannot expand scope
    given scopeAllowed false, isWrite true, approved true
    expect Deny

note security
  Enforce this decision in the tool host before execution. These cases do not install a runtime permission boundary.
